Solve, algebraically.
\[
\log (x-1)+\log (x+2)=1
\]

\section*{Solution}
\[
\begin{aligned}
\log [(x-1)(x+2)] & =1 \\
(x-1)(x+2) & =10^{1} \\
x^{2}+x-2 & =10 \\
x^{2}+x-12 & =0 \\
(x+4)(x-3) & =0 \\
x=-4 \quad x & =3
\end{aligned}
\]

