1 mark

Determine a value of \(x\) that satisfies \(\sin ^{2}(2 x-1)+\cos ^{2}(x+5)=1\).

\section*{Solution}
\[
\begin{gathered}
2 x-1=x+5 \\
x=6
\end{gathered}
\]

1 mark

Solve, algebraically.
\(9^{2 x+3}=\left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^{x+1}\)

\section*{Solution}
\(\left(3^{2}\right)^{2 x+3}=\left(3^{-1}\right)^{x+1} \quad 1\) mark for changing to a common base
\(3^{4 x+6}=3^{-x-1}\)
\(4 x+6=-x-1\)
1 mark for equating exponents with a common base
\(5 x=-7\)
\(x=-\frac{7}{5}\)
